[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (5,0);
\coordinate (B) at (1.8,2.8);
\coordinate (D) at (1.8,0);
\draw (A) -- (C) node[midway, below] {$b$};
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, above left] {$c$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, above right] {$a$};
\draw[dashed] (B) -- (D) node[midway, right] {$h$};
\draw (1.8,0.3) -- (2.1,0.3) -- (2.1,0);
\pic[draw, "$C$", angle radius=0.6cm, angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=B--C--A};
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above] at (B) {$B$};
\node[below right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[below] at (D) {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
In $\Delta ABC$, an altitude $BD = h$ is drawn perpendicular to base $AC = b$. Using right-angled triangle $\Delta BCD$, express $h$ in terms of $a$ and $C$, and hence show that $\text{Area} = \dfrac{1}{2}ab\sin C$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (5.2,0);
\coordinate (C) at (2.2,3.0);
\coordinate (D) at (2.2,0);
\draw (A) -- (B);
\draw (A) -- (C) node[midway, above left] {$b$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, above right] {$a$};
\draw[dashed] (C) -- (D) node[midway, left] {$h$};
\draw (2.2,0.3) -- (2.5,0.3) -- (2.5,0);
\pic[draw, "$A$", angle radius=0.6cm, angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=B--A--C};
\pic[draw, "$B$", angle radius=0.6cm, angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=C--B--A};
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above] at (C) {$C$};
\node[below] at (D) {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
In $\Delta ABC$, altitude $CD = h$ is drawn perpendicular to $AB$. Express $h$ in terms of $A$ and $b$, then in terms of $B$ and $a$. Equate both expressions to derive the sine rule $\dfrac{a}{\sin A} = \dfrac{b}{\sin B}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (5.5,0);
\coordinate (C) at (2.0,2.8);
\coordinate (D) at (2.0,0);
\draw (A) -- (D) node[midway, below] {$x$};
\draw (D) -- (B) node[midway, below] {$c-x$};
\draw (A) -- (C) node[midway, above left] {$b$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, above right] {$a$};
\draw[dashed] (C) -- (D) node[midway, left] {$h$};
\draw (2.0,0.3) -- (2.3,0.3) -- (2.3,0);
\pic[draw, "$A$", angle radius=0.6cm, angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=B--A--C};
